  "notes": [
    "Reflexive -AR verb with a spelling change: *c→qu* before *e*, to preserve the hard /k/ sound — affects the yo form of Pretérito Indefinido (*me fabriqué*, not *me fabricé*) and all of Subjuntivo Presente (*me fabrique, te fabriques...*)",
    "Same spelling pattern as *dedicarse*, *comunicar*, *secar*",
    "Affirmative imperative attaches the reflexive pronoun with a written accent to preserve stress (*fabrícate, fabríquese, fabriquémonos, fabríquense*); negative imperative places the pronoun separately (*no te fabriques*...)",
    "Past participle: *fabricado* (regular)",
    "Two main senses: reflexive \"to make/build for oneself\" — *se fabricó su propia casa* (he built his own house) — and passive-reflexive \"to be manufactured\" — *este producto se fabrica en España* (this product is manufactured in Spain)",
    "Base verb *fabricar* (\"to manufacture, to make\") is the non-reflexive counterpart, worth adding separately if needed",
    "Related: *fábrica* (factory), *fabricante* (manufacturer), *fabricación* (manufacturing)"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/f/Fabricarse.md"
